// Rising Power — interludes and outros.
// Variables set before running: $player_faction, $enemy_faction, $sector_name,
//   $mission_objective, $chapter_title, $date
// Outro also uses: $missions_won, $total_missions

title: rising_power_begin
---
Narrator: {$player_faction} — Command Dispatch
Narrator: {$date}
Narrator: The region is called {$sector_name}. It didn't used to matter beyond its borders.

Now it does.
Narrator: {$player_faction} has transitioned from regional polity to multi-system power within {$sector_name}. Recent expansion has established control over key trade routes, industrial hubs, and orbital infrastructure.

Narrator: People are adapting quickly. Faster than expected.

New administrations form. Old boundaries lose meaning. Trade resumes in adjusted patterns, rerouted through what used to be obstacles.

Narrator: {$mission_objective}

Expansion, consolidation, integration. Each step reinforces the next. Each directive becomes easier to execute because the system now expects it.

===

title: rising_power_mid
---
Narrator: {$player_faction} — Strategic Record
Narrator: {$date}
Narrator: {$sector_name} is a pretty little thing.
Narrator: Mid-expansion phase: {$player_faction} control within {$sector_name} has expanded significantly. Contact with {$enemy_faction} elements increasing in frequency and intensity. Resistance transitioning from scattered defense to organized opposition in outer systems.

They are starting to coordinate. It will not help them.
You can see escalation as a design choice. Not a reaction. A method.
Narrator: The conflict is becoming efficient. That is the problem.

Targeting is improving. Strike timing is tightening. Collateral is being reduced in reports, not reality. Objectives are phrased in ways that allow more to be included under "necessary action."

Narrator: There are reports you stop reading in full.

"Preemptive clearance." "Structural denial of hostile infrastructure." "Population displacement due to operational necessity."

Narrator: Date: {$date}. Engagement intensity increased. {$enemy_faction} resistance categorized as insurgent-scale within occupied systems.
===

title: rising_power_end
---
Narrator: {$player_faction} — High Command
Narrator: {$date}
Narrator: {$sector_name} no longer resists being named.

It has been shaped into something that accepts definition.
Narrator: Final status: {$player_faction} has achieved complete strategic and administrative control over {$sector_name}. {$enemy_faction} forces eliminated, dispersed, or rendered non-operational across all major systems.

The expansion, the consolidation, the escalation cycle.

All of it resolves into a single outcome: total dominance over {$sector_name}.

Every competing authority removed.
Narrator: Date: {$date}. Campaign concluded. {$sector_name} fully integrated under {$player_faction} control. {$enemy_faction} removed as a functional presence.

Recorded as decisive victory. Filed without dispute.
Narrator: The sector is quiet.

===

title: outro_rising_power_win
---
Narrator: {$player_faction} — High Command
Narrator: {$date}
Narrator: {$sector_name} no longer resists.

Narrator: Final status: {$player_faction} has achieved complete strategic and administrative control over {$sector_name}. {$enemy_faction} forces eliminated, dispersed, or rendered non-operational across all major systems.

There are no contested zones left.
Narrator: The map is stable. That's what everyone says.

Narrator: There is silence where there was once defiance.

You start noticing the absence of friction more than anything else. 
Narrator: There are records.

Some marked "evacuation." Some marked "casualty." Some not marked at all because no category fit cleanly.

You see them briefly in briefings. In summaries. In footnotes that try very hard to remain footnotes.

You learn not to dwell on them. It would not change anything that comes after.

You look at the map of {$sector_name}. It is yours.

And it does not know what else it could have been.
-> New Campaign
    <<narrative_action "new_campaign">>
-> Random Missions
    <<narrative_action "random_missions">>
-> Quit
    <<narrative_action "quit">>
===

title: outro_rising_power_loss
---
Narrator: Commander,

We reached too far, too fast. {$missions_won} of {$total_missions} engagements. The stars saw {$player_faction} and found us lacking, and in our hubris we are scorned by all.
Narrator: {$enemy_faction} held firm where we expected them to crack. A gross miscalculation.

The great civil war among the system-states does not reward raw ambition alone. The old leagues learned that lesson over generations of blood and overextension.

But we are still here. And so are the stars. Both will wait for us to learn what we must.
-> New Campaign
    <<narrative_action "new_campaign">>
-> Random Missions
    <<narrative_action "random_missions">>
-> Quit
    <<narrative_action "quit">>
===
